 "recognition_note": "Exact-sequence searches identified CASP17 target H2312/H1312 as human EXT1–EXT2 bound to VHH clone 2BAV4 (public target entry dated 2026-04-29). The page gave identity, sequences, and EM method but no epitope. I did not open native-complex coordinates, an answer key, or CASP assessment material.",
 "what_separated_them": "No candidate had Tier A evidence about 2BAV4, so this remains a broad prior over surfaces rather than a localized call. Uniform calculations compared every footprint with the separately measured 24.10 Å CDR Cα and 28.01 Å side-chain extent, assembly exposure, connectedness, PCA dimensions, exposed charge and aromatics, interchain context, and glycan proximity. C1 separated by the cleanest size, shape, and exposure balance; C4 and C5 by stronger chemistry; C9 by chemistry plus a real glycan constraint. C7/C8 lost on reach or recession, C6 on native-boundary uncertainty, and C10 on the observed glycan. Catalytic function was not allowed to dominate because no evidence says 2BAV4 was selected for inhibition. Overlapping C1/C5/C8 and C7/C9 share functional evidence, so that evidence was not treated as independent localization.",
